  equilibrium that would 'decouple' at z* is the PHANTOM -- the isothermal
  phase of the charge in the DEEP regime (g_ext < a0), i.e. the equilibrium
  inside galaxies.  Its temperature scale is the GALACTIC virial dispersion,
  the triad sigma = 119.2 km/s (sigma^2 = v_flat^2/2, G151).  Clusters sit
  49x ABOVE the EFE line ((cH0/a0)^2 = 49, G093 E1): they host the FREE dust,
  no equilibrium, nothing to decouple -- a cluster-class sigma describes a
  phase that never forms.  The headline curve therefore uses the canonical
  triad sigma 119.2; the other footings bracket it; the cluster class is
  run to SHOW the failure mode (it is the which-sigma discriminator).

