--- PART 3 THE TENSION: z* = 2.4 + the G080 high-z test (z ~ 2.5) ---
  G080 (MSA-3D, 30 galaxies, z = 0.58-1.68): log10(v_obs/v_pred) median flat,
  weighted slope |t| < 2, zero point z-INDEPENDENT -- the law holds BELOW the
  formation epoch, as the equilibrium picture requires (z < z*: the phantom
  exists, the BTFR zero point is flat at 0.00).
  G011/G080 discriminator: at z = 2.5 the registered rising-a0 target is +0.33 dex vs flat 0.00 (floor 0.13).
  G132 z* band: 2.37-2.49.  THE EPOCHS COINCIDE: the discriminator z = 2.5
  sits 0.01-0.13 z ABOVE the formation band -- the G011 window IS the z_break
  window.  The z~2.5 test is therefore not only the a0-evolution funnel it was
  registered as; it is the equilibrium-FORMATION epoch test.
  SHARPENED PREDICTION: IF the equilibrium forms at z* ~ 2.4-2.5, the BTFR
  zero point is FLAT below z* (G080's data already show this to 1.68) and
  BEGINS to evolve AT z* -- a break/turn-on at z in [2.37, 2.5], not a smooth
  drift from z = 0 (which the flat G080 trend already excludes at 1-1.7 z).
  The measured break epoch z_break IS the measurement of z*; the cross-check
  is the inversion: z_break ~ 2.4 -> m ~ 5.05 keV (canonical) inside the
  forest window.  One observable (BTFR zero point vs z) ends in a particle
  mass: the framework predicts the BTFR zero point's evolution BEGINS at z*,
  with the z* -> m consistency as the cross-check.

